  partName: Rear Blade
  description: The Rear Blade is a tiny, elongated component positioned at the middle-rear
    center of the engine, made from Blades texture material. As the third blade in
    the turbine section, it further contributes to the engine's energy extraction
    process, working in tandem with the Rear Blade and to produce mechanical energy.
    Notably, its placement at the rear of the engine allows it to take advantage
    of the exhaust gases' remaining energy potential.
